{# Forward-built for Task 30 (`PasswordResetService`), per Task 29's own
   scope note: the template exists and follows the exact same
   subject/text/html-block convention as `verify_email.html.twig` (see that
   file's comment for why), but nothing dispatches `SendEmailMessage` with a
   reset-password template identifier yet -- there is no
   `SendEmailMessage::TEMPLATE_RESET_PASSWORD` constant and no matching case
   in `App\MessageHandler\SendEmailMessageHandler` until Task 30 adds both.
   This file is inert until then.

   Context (once wired): `resetUrl` (an absolute URL to the reset-password
   completion route, carrying the reset token). #}
{% if false %}
    {% block subject %}Reset your password{% endblock %}
    {% block text %}
Hello,

We received a request to reset your password. Open the link below to choose a new one:

{{ resetUrl }}

This link expires in 1 hour. If you did not request this, you can safely ignore this email --
your password will not be changed.
    {% endblock %}
{% endif %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <title>{{ block('subject') }}</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <p>Hello,</p>
        <p>We received a request to reset your password. Click the link below to choose a new one:</p>
        <p><a href="{{ resetUrl }}">Reset your password</a></p>
        <p>This link expires in 1 hour. If you did not request this, you can safely ignore this email
        &mdash; your password will not be changed.</p>
    </body>
</html>
